  holding="Under article I, section 7, a warrantless vehicle search incident to arrest is allowed only when needed for officer safety or to preserve evidence of the arrest crime that could be concealed or destroyed. Once the arrestee is secured and can't reach the car, the exception doesn't apply; get a warrant or use another exception.",
